    <string name="advanced_title">Advanced settings</string>
    <string name="advanced_subtitle">They change how the model behaves. They take effect from the next scene.</string>
    <string name="advanced_engine_on">Engine on</string>
    <string name="advanced_engine_on_text">Switch it off to always play with the original text of the book, with no translation and no enrichment. It stays off even if you close and reopen the app, until you press "Activate" on a model or turn it back on here.</string>
    <string name="advanced_translation_mode">Translation mode</string>
    <string name="advanced_translation_mode_text">Gemma only translates the text of the book with the smallest possible changes, without enriching it. Lighter to generate. It switches off the controls below (a fixed preset takes their place): the text changes from the next scene, the parameters from the next load of the model.</string>
    <string name="advanced_max_tokens">Maximum tokens</string>
    <string name="advanced_max_tokens_text">How long the context of a scene may be. High values allow longer texts but eat more memory and time. Impact on CPU/memory: medium.</string>
    <string name="advanced_temperature">Temperature (creativity)</string>
    <string name="advanced_temperature_text">High values (0.9) make the prose more creative, low values (0.2) more faithful and predictable. Impact on CPU/memory: none.</string>
    <string name="advanced_top_p">Top-P (nucleus sampling)</string>
    <string name="advanced_top_p_text">A high value (0.95) considers more words, a low one is more restrictive. Impact on CPU/memory: low.</string>
    <string name="advanced_top_k">Top-K (vocabulary sampling)</string>
    <string name="advanced_top_k_text">Considers only the K most likely words. High (50) gives more variety, low (10) is more cautious. Impact on CPU/memory: low.</string>
    <string name="advanced_model_picks_background">The model picks the background</string>
    <string name="advanced_model_picks_background_text">When a scene has no background declared by the book, ask the model to suggest one from a closed list — it makes the prompt longer. Off by default: only what the book declares is used. Handy for comparing different models.</string>
